<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbundantĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		abundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abundance</i>, <i>plenty</i>, <i>fulness</i>, <i>richness</i> (syn. copia).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In the Cic. and Aug.
			per. usu. with a <i>gen.</i> to define it more
			exactly: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium rerum abundantia et copia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Lael. 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Agr. 2, 97</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">otii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
					7, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 9, 1</span></i>
			 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i>pecuniary wealth</i>, <i>riches</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Cat. 2, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. Agr.
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 2, 94</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laborare abundantiā,</span>”
				<i>from overloading the stomach</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 44</span></i>
			 (cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib.
			40</span></i>).—Fig., of speech: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multa ex juvenili abundantiā
					coërcuisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 1, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
